", :adr/decision "{:new_org {:name \"jk-luxury\", :repos_edn_orgs_entry {:role :human-centric, :scope :business}, :rationale \"GitHub home for the JK株式会社 legal entity, carved out of gftdcojp (Gftd Japan\\n              株式会社) for adult-content/creator-economy products, matching the pre-existing\\n              informal entity split\"}, :transfer {:what \"club-shinshi and net-babiniku transferred gftdcojp -> jk-luxury via\\n          gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/transfer, remaining private\", :local_checkouts \"orgs/gftdcojp/{club-shinshi,net-babiniku} moved to\\n                     orgs/jk-luxury/{club-shinshi,net-babiniku}, matching the established\\n                     path-override precedent for every prior GitHub-org transfer in this repo\\n                     (manimani->gftdcojp, cloud-manimani->gftdcojp,\\n                     cloud-murakumo->local-murakumo, kototama->kotoba-lang)\"}, :repos_edn_path_overrides [\"orgs/gftdcojp/club-shinshi -> orgs/jk-luxury/club-shinshi\" \"orgs/gftdcojp/net-babiniku -> orgs/jk-luxury/net-babiniku\"], :extra_projects_entry_unchanged \"net-babiniku's original :extra-projects entry (registered\\n                                   under ADR-2607051800) is left textually unchanged -- the\\n                                   override is the record of the subsequent move, not a\\n                                   rewrite of history\", :west_yml_regeneration \"nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry club-shinshi --entry\\n                          net-babiniku -- minimal-diff, not a wholesale regeneration, per\\n                          ADR-2607022900\", :payment_rail_amendment {:what \"net-babiniku's monetization launches with ONLY the crypto/USDC rail, not the\\n          fiat/adult-PSP rail ADR-2607062200 specified as primary\", :boundary_unchanged \"self-custody on-chain settlement code still may not be scaffolded in\\n                       net-babiniku itself -- the vendor/etzhayyim centralization-axis\\n                       boundary (ADR-2605211950, ADR-2605172100) was never gftdcojp-specific,\\n                       it applies to any vendor-side repo, jk-luxury included. Actual\\n                       settlement logic must still live in etzhayyim/root, consumed via a\\n                       consent-capability boundary; net-babiniku implements only the domain\\n                       model/governor/ledger/UI that call into that capability\", :chain_custody_undecided \"concrete chain/wallet-custody choice is NOT decided by this ADR\\n                             -- building real fund-moving code without that input would be\\n                             premature; this round's implementation stubs the actual\\n                             settlement call behind the same honest-default/no-fake-checkout\\n                             pattern ADR-2607062200 already established for the fiat rail\"}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"user direction 2026-07-06: created https://github.com/jk-luxury, directed that\\n           club-shinshi and net-babiniku be relocated there, private; separately, directed\\n           crypto-only payment rail for now (narrower than ADR-2607062200's fiat-primary\\n           decision)\", :pre_existing_split \"gftd-talent-actor docs already note 'itonami (Gftd Japan株式会社,\\n                       cloud-itonami) serves club-shinshi (JK株式会社)' -- club-shinshi was\\n                       already operated under a different legal entity than the rest of\\n                       gftdcojp, even though its repo lived under the gftdcojp GitHub org\", :why_now \"both club-shinshi and net-babiniku are adult-content-adjacent creator-economy\\n            products (ADR-2607062200, ADR-2607062210 land in the same session); giving them\\n            their own org boundary scopes any future PSP/compliance audit surface cleanly,\\n            separate from gftdcojp's other business lines\", :risk_check {:club_shinshi \"private, no .github/workflows/, no webhooks -- deploys are manual CLI\", :net_babiniku \"private, no .github/workflows/, no webhooks -- deploys via `wrangler pages\\n                  deploy`, no custom domain bound (net-babiniku.pages.dev)\", :conclusion \"no GitHub-App-triggered CI/CD exists for either repo, so an org transfer\\n               carries materially lower operational risk than it would for a repo with\\n               org-scoped Actions secrets or a GitHub-App-linked deploy pipeline\"}}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"keep both repos under gftdcojp, rely on repo-level access control only\", :rejected_because \"the org itself is the natural boundary for an already-distinct legal\\n                      entity (JK株式会社); the informal split was already on record, this\\n                      just makes the GitHub structure match it\"} {:option \"create fresh repos under jk-luxury with clean history instead of transferring\", :rejected_because \"a GitHub transfer preserves issues/stars/history and both repos are\\n                      recent/small with no CI coupling to lose; a clean-history split made\\n                      sense for club-shinshi's original monorepo extraction but is\\n                      unnecessary overhead for an org-only move of already-standalone repos\"} {:option \"silently rewrite the existing :extra-projects entry's path instead of adding a\\n            :path-overrides entry\", :rejected_because \"every prior GitHub-org transfer in this repo used :path-overrides with\\n                      a dated rationale comment, preserving the original registration\\n                      decision's text; breaking that convention here would lose the audit\\n                      trail this repo otherwise maintains carefully\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607062300: new GitHub org jk-luxury -- relocate club-shinshi and net-babiniku\n          out of gftdcojp; crypto-only payment rail for now", :adr/source-format "edn"}]